	file.0000000000000001.title: "Cobblemon: aBunchaMods"
	quest.03F8B40FE7F14849.quest_desc: ["Wireless Terminals are the exact same as the normal terminal equilivent but wireless!"]
	quest.06F8F145D1583F23.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.06F8F145D1583F23.quest_subtitle: "Catch 4 More Pokemon to Build a Team!"
	quest.07B89EF627CA6824.quest_desc: [
		"To Claim a Chunk Press M or Go to Your Inventory and Click the Map in the Top Left"
		""
		"From there you can drag your mouse around and claim the land around you."
		""
		"To Force load (like OG Chunk Loaders) Shift-Left click the chunk and if you did it right it will have lines across the chunk."
		""
		"To unclaim land do the same but hold right click or shift right click on the claimed chunks. "
	]
	quest.0C02A39661CAEEE3.quest_desc: ["Arguably the most important aspect of Applied Energistics 2 is its storage system, making use of digital &eStorage Cells&f. These cells are accessible through either an &eME Chest&r for single cells, or an &eME Drive&r for multiple cells.\\n\\nThe &bME Chest&f holds a single Cell at a time, which can then be read from and written to from any other terminal on the same network. The ME Chest itself also provides its own terminal screen on the top with specific access only to the cell it contains.\\n\\nThe &bME Drive&f can hold up to 10 assorted Storage Cells in the space of a single block and a single ME channel. However, it does not provide its own terminal screen, requiring some external terminal elsewhere on the network for storage access."]
	quest.149C428E2DD03173.quest_desc: ["a 25% Drop Chance from Articuno, Moltres, and Zapdos"]
	quest.196135905C3FB8C6.quest_subtitle: "Catch some PokeMon!"
	quest.1A2907B2912877B6.quest_desc: ["Welcome to Cobblemon: aBunchaMods a ModPack similiar to ATM10 without the super OP mods!"]
	quest.1AEE730F867D2E11.quest_subtitle: "Craft an Ultra Ball!"
	quest.1AEE730F867D2E11.title: "Craft an Ultra Ball!"
	quest.1E6D907242530577.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Great Ball!"
	quest.1E6D907242530577.title: "Craft a Great Ball"
	quest.1E995B862F0AE98C.quest_desc: ["These work the same as other cables however they will display the amount of channels in use as colored lines along the cables."]
	quest.1E995B862F0AE98C.title: "Advanced Cables"
	quest.237D1B02B0893CAE.quest_desc: [
		"&3Certus Quartz&f are needed for basically everything in Ae2."
		""
		"You can grow them forever with Flawless Budding Certus Quartz (and u can steal these from meteors with a cardboard box O_O)"
		""
		"Find these and then mine the Quartz they grow to get the Certus Quartz Dust and Crystals you need."
	]
	quest.255B67E6C830F1B6.quest_desc: [
		"Terminals give access to the contents of your ME network."
		""
		""
		"The ME Crafting Terminal also has a built in crafting grid."
	]
	quest.2D6AFCD1270AC75D.quest_subtitle: "Use Every Lure Type!"
	quest.2F3DCFB10DEEF700.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have all the Inscriber Presses, get to work on making some Processors."
		""
		"These are essential to crafting most Ae2 devices."
	]
	quest.2F3DCFB10DEEF700.title: "Processors"
	quest.2F5118C4576D0155.quest_desc: ["By default, an ME network on its own only has an internal buffer of 800AE without an ME Controller, with the controller adding an extra 8kAE per block. For large enough networks, this can be insufficient and may cause a network to power off intermittently when trying to recoup power for any connected devices.\\n\\nThe &bEnergy Cell&f allows for an ME network to hold significantly more energy, adding another 200kAE per regular Energy Cell and 1.6MAE per &bDense&f Energy Cell. These can also be placed anywhere in the network to provide the increased energy buffer."]
	quest.309344E43A3619E5.quest_desc: ["Once you have a storage drive pop it into the ME Drive you made earlier and you can start putting items in your system through a Terminal"]
	quest.3904FCE72AD28292.quest_desc: [
		"To get started with AE2 you are going to need a &3Charger&f and &5Inscriber&f."
		""
		"The &3Charger&f, when powered will charge Certus Quartz Crystals and charge them."
		"With the Charged Crystals they can be used to make Fluix Crystals."
		""
		"The &5Inscriber&fis used to turn different crystals into their dust forms, but their #1 use is to"
		"use the &5Inscriber &fto create &cPrinted Circuits &fand &cProcessors&f."
	]
	quest.3904FCE72AD28292.quest_subtitle: "Lets Roll!"
	quest.3904FCE72AD28292.title: "Getting Started"
	quest.3B75D64302BCB50B.quest_desc: ["The final goal of the modpack is to craft the Masters Star."]
	quest.449652FB57155835.quest_desc: [
		"Meteorites can be found around your world that contain Sky Stone."
		""
		"Dig into them to find a Mysterious Cube"
		""
		"Once you have dug into the cube you will have all the Presses you need."
		""
		"If you are having trouble finding a Meteorite you can craft a &cMeteorite Compass&f to lead you to one."
	]
	quest.449652FB57155835.quest_subtitle: "Find the Meteorites"
	quest.449652FB57155835.title: "Meteorites"
	quest.4BD84369B1A67780.quest_desc: ["Kill God: a 100% Drop Chance from Killing Arceus WITH a sword."]
	quest.4BD84369B1A67780.title: "Kill God"
	quest.50F8B11EB1197810.quest_desc: [
		"The Inscriber and Charger will accept RF/FE energy, but the Ae2 uses its own power system called AE."
		""
		"Plug in RF/FE energy to the Energy Acceptor to convert RF/FE at a ratio of 2:1 you can also plug directly into an ME Controller."
	]
	quest.531EFE286CC7D077.quest_desc: ["Craft a Fast Ball, Level Ball, Lure Ball, Heavy Ball, Love Ball, Friend Ball, and a Moon Ball"]
	quest.531EFE286CC7D077.title: "Craft all Apricorn Balls"
	quest.56A39F86EF2E6FB2.quest_desc: ["To connect the vast majority of your ME network together, you will need some cable. &eME Glass Cable&f is the first and most basic kind of cable, and you'll be making this all throughout as the first step towards crafting the other kinds of cable.\\n\\nBoth glass cables and their &ecovered&f counterpart can carry up to 8 channels along a single section of cabling. Unlike glass cables, covered cables can subsequently be crafted into &edense&f covered cables, capable of carrying up to 32 channels. However, most 'multipart' devices such as buses and terminals cannot be directly attached to dense cables, requiring normal-width cables to form a connection instead.\\n\\nAll cables can also be crafted with dye to colour them. Uncoloured ('Fluix') cables can connect to any other colour of cable, but otherwise differently-coloured cables will never connect to one another."]
	quest.56A39F86EF2E6FB2.title: "Cables"
	quest.57349D1DEC37DFD6.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to &l&3Applied Energistics 2"
		""
		"Applied Energistics 2 is a digital storage mod, allowing for storage and automation"
		""
		""
		"For more info check out &zappliedenergistics.github.io"
	]
	quest.57349D1DEC37DFD6.quest_subtitle: "Virtual Storage System"
	quest.5835BF0AFF942E3D.quest_subtitle: "Place a Campfire Pot onto a Campfire and get cooking!"
	quest.58B125BD4876054C.title: "Mekanism!"
	quest.592EF41146E23E2B.quest_subtitle: "Catch your first Shiny!"
	quest.6078078EE009AA33.quest_desc: ["Energy Cards can be inserted into most devices to increase their energy buffer."]
	quest.61D2463AFD8327DF.quest_desc: [
		"You will notice the max level of PokeMon you can level is level 15. To Go past this find a Village and find the Pokemon Association villager there. You can now trade him your trainer card to start your quest."
		""
		""
		"Radical Red is Very Hard"
		""
		""
		"RCT Wiki is also a very valuable resource if you are confused on how to level "
		""
		"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/rctmod"
		""
		"www.srcmc.gitlab.io/rct/docs/0.16/gameplay/progression/#level-cap"
	]
	quest.61D2463AFD8327DF.title: "Leveling Past Level 15"
	quest.63C3A711C685B4C5.quest_desc: ["Boost the wireless range to be infinite and access your ME system in any dimension!"]
	quest.685F34837B351B7C.quest_desc: ["a 75% Drop Chance from MewTwo"]
	quest.69DAF6ADF4D9E7D7.quest_desc: ["Craft a PokeBall, Citrine Ball, Verdant Ball, Azure Ball, Roseate Ball, Slate Ball, and a Premier Ball"]
	quest.69DAF6ADF4D9E7D7.quest_subtitle: "Craft all Basic Colored PokeBalls!"
	quest.69DAF6ADF4D9E7D7.title: "Craft Basic PokeBalls"
	quest.6F603C6E9AEB68C1.quest_desc: ["To make your network wireless create the ME Wireless Access Point and connect it to your network."]
	quest.743668DC922171D8.quest_desc: ["Quartz Wrench acts as a normal wrench. Can rotate blocks/devices and break them while Sneak Right Clicking."]
	quest.744A6EFBCD917F10.quest_desc: ["Partition Drives to Hold Specific Items"]
	quest.758DBC0B99C4944E.quest_desc: ["Apricots can be found littered around the world on apricot trees, right click to harvest them and begin a pokeball farm"]
	quest.758DBC0B99C4944E.quest_subtitle: "Find Red and White Apricots and Make Pokeballs"
	quest.758DBC0B99C4944E.title: "Craft A PokeBall"
	quest.76C18C45D0116429.quest_desc: [
		"Arguably the most important resource you will need next is &eFluix&f, used throughout the vast majority of AE2 devices and serving as a base for crafting all of the cabling within an ME network. "
		""
		"You'll typically want to mass produce these, and the way to do so is to make a &bFluix Crystal&f by throwing &eNether Quartz&f, &e&oCharged&r&e Certus quartz&r and &eRedstone&f together in a pool of water. This will give you a &eFluix Crystal&r which you can turn to dust in an Inscriber."
	]
	quest.774EDCEB8FA9331C.quest_desc: [
		"Some basic commands that can help you out are"
		""
		"/sethome (name of home) - Lets you set a home where you are standing to teleport back/forth ex /sethome Cave - Use /home"
		"to go back to that home"
		""
		"/spawn - Teleport to the world spawn"
		""
		"/back - go back to your last location before teleporting"
		""
		""
		""
		"(Multiplayer)"
		""
		"/tpa (friends username)   - for ex /tpa Wild1n would send a teleport requst to the user Wild1n"
		""
		"/tpahere (friends username) - Will send your friend a request to teleport to you"
		""
		""
		"By default only one home is available, to add more homes go to your save/(name of save)/serverconfig/ftbessentials.snbt"
	]
	quest.7A00F7F7E4D40631.quest_desc: [
		"Each Cell has a certain capacity based on the component that the cell was crafted with"
		""
		""
		"The lowest component is the 1k ME Sotrage Component. Providing 1024 bytes of storage."
	]
	quest.7A00F7F7E4D40631.title: "Creating Storage Cells"
	quest.7D07D8BFA7658E1A.quest_desc: ["Poké Rods are obtained via a Smithing Table using any Poké Ball, a Fishing Rod and a Poké Rod Upgrade Smithing Template."]
	quest.7D07D8BFA7658E1A.quest_subtitle: "Trade With Villagers or Loot Ruin Structures to Find the Template!"
	quest.7DB5FABCCBD7F301.quest_desc: ["an 85% Drop Chance from Rayquaza"]
	quest.7EBAB495879E5F20.quest_desc: [
		"The last piece of the puzzle for any large ME network is the &bME Controller&f. "
		""
		"A controller supplies an ME Network with a far larger number of channels than the standard 8 channels for ad-hoc networks, providing 32 channels out of each face of the block for a total of 216 channels. "
		""
		"That's only for a single-block controller, however, since the ME Controller is in fact a multi-block structure. The controller can be up to 7x7x7 blocks in size and can come in any freeform arrangement within that maximum size. Each individual block can then provide its own separate set of channels, so long as no single controller block is surrounded by 4 other blocks along the same plane. "
		""
		"An ME Network may only contain one multiblock controller at any given time. Attempting to connect more than one controller on separate parts of the network will cause a conflict, shutting down the whole network."
	]
